eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-9 : List Word
eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-9 = unlines (cons "In “Eye Contact: Co-Processing at the Speed of Light” (Part 7 of the Information Dynamic series), on the visual processing pipeline through which eye contact couples two nervous systems:" (cons "The Visual Processing Pipeline" (cons "Understanding what's being coupled:" (cons "When light from Person A's face reaches Person B's retina:" (cons "1. Photoreceptor array (~100+ million rods and cones)" (cons "Transduces photon flux to electrical signals" (cons "Preserves 2D spatial structure and spectral (color) information" (cons "This is brain tissue directly responding to electromagnetic field" (cons "2. Retinal processing layers" (cons "Horizontal cells, amacrine cells, bipolar cells" (cons "Perform edge detection, motion detection, contrast enhancement" (cons "First quotient operation: 100M+ inputs → ~1M outputs (retinal ganglion cells)" (cons "This computation happens in the eye (brain tissue) before signals leave" (cons "3. Optic nerve → Lateral Geniculate Nucleus" (cons "Signals transmitted to thalamus" (cons "Further processing and relay" (cons "Massive feedback from cortex (more backward connections than forward)" (cons "4. Primary Visual Cortex (V1)" (cons "Extracts oriented edges, motion direction, binocular disparity" (cons "Organized in orientation columns (neurons selective for specific angles)" (cons "Second major quotient: spatial information → edge/orientation features" (cons "5. Higher visual areas (V2, V4, IT, MT)" (cons "Build increasingly abstract representations" (cons "V2: edge combinations, simple shapes" (cons "V4: complex shapes, color constancy" (cons "IT (inferotemporal): object categories, faces, specific individuals" (cons "MT: motion patterns, biological motion" (cons "Each stage is quotient operation compressing information while preserving structure relevant for recognition and prediction." nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
